# Keep the Docker build context small and the build deterministic.
target/
# .git stays out of the context, with one exception: build.rs stamps the commit
# SHA into the binary, and inside the image there is no other way to learn it.
# Render exposes RENDER_GIT_COMMIT to the build too, but its docs are not
# explicit about whether that reaches a Dockerfile as a build arg, so the three
# files below are re-included to make the SHA derivable from the context alone.
# They are a few hundred bytes; the rest of .git (objects, logs) stays excluded.
.git/
!.git/HEAD
!.git/refs/
!.git/refs/**
!.git/packed-refs
.github/
.devcontainer/
node_modules/
*.md
!README.md
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.editorconfig
rustfmt.toml
LICENSE
